# --- Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest ----------------------------------------------------------------
info title=Sealkeeper Spire
info author=Custom Islands
info description=The Network's control spire in a storm over the trench: a generator, ziplines to the pump and door towers, fuses, a keypad - and two levers, RESTORE and SEAL. The ninth island of The Sunken Kingdom, the first half of its finale.
island on.arrive=message||A stone spire in the storm, a cable from its top running down into the sea.

story power|Base power on|Battery|You started the Spire's generator.
story pumped|Pumps primed|Hinge|You cranked the pump tower's valve: the Commons' pumps have pressure.
story fuse|Spire fuse|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|A ceramic fuse from the door tower's lockers.
story fused|Fuse board set|Battery|You set the fuses: the spire's windows are lit.
story unlocked|Control room unlocked|Battery|You keyed the Commons' code into the control room's keypad.
story winched|Cable wound|Hinge|You wound the cable winch: the cable head is live.
story chosen|The choice made|Bolt|You pulled one of the two levers at the cable head.
story descended|Descend lever|Bolt|You pulled the descend lever.
story restorechoice|RESTORE pulled|Bolt|You chose RESTORE at the Sealkeeper Spire.
story sealchoice|SEAL pulled|Bolt|You chose SEAL at the Sealkeeper Spire.

note milocard Milo's crayon card | A CARD IN CRAYON, WEDGED IN THE DOCK RAIL\n\nTO MUM.\nWe are on the plane!!! The plane man says it is the last one. Mr Fennick is not coming, he says somebody has to close a door properly. He gave me his hat.\nThere were 12 of us and we are all here, I counted twice like you said.\nI did not have Mo. A man at the yard said he would keep him. If you find him tell him I am OK.\nI am going to Gran's on the high island. Come and get me after.\nLOVE MILO (age 7)\n(a drawing of a whale, a plane and a very tall lady with a diving mask)
note confession The Director's confession | DIRECTOR HALVARD ROOK - FOR WHOEVER COMES UP THE LADDER\n\nIt hunts what is lit and what is loud. We learned that the night the doors were open and it came up the trench pipe. The Commons was the brightest, loudest room in the sea - four hundred people, every family of the Network.\nSo I made the rest of the sea brighter and louder than them. No. I made the rest of the sea go dark, one station at a time, and I left one light burning far away, on the roofs, so it would swim there instead. The Spirecrest beacon. The one you answered.\nI drowned Brinelab. I opened sluice 4 with eight men in the store. I sent divers to cut their own cables, and three crews did not come back. I did the sums every night and every night they came out the same: forty-one people for four hundred.\nI sent the children up. Fennick made me. I am glad he did.\nInes will tell you I am a murderer. She is right. She will also tell you the Commons is alive. She is right about that too.\nThe levers are on the shore. RESTORE, and the lights come back and the Commons can leave - and it will come up to the lights. SEAL, and the plug drops on the Hollow, and the Network stays dark for ever.\nI could not choose. I am handing it to you. I am sorry about that too.
prop skcam obj.name=skcam
prop sklure obj.name=sklure
prop sklure beh.hidden=1
prop sklure tint.color=#2fd0c0
prop sklure tint.amount=0.8
prop sklure beh.move=-28,0,-14
prop sklure beh.moveTime=20
prop sklure beh.moveMode=switch
note orders Sealkeeper's orders | SEALKEEPER'S ORDERS - DIRECTOR H. ROOK\n\n1. Power first: the generator on the base.\n2. Prime the pumps from the pump tower. Fuses from the door tower.\n3. The control room is keyed with the Commons' code.\n4. Wind the cable. At the cable head: RESTORE, or SEAL. Not both. There is no both.\n5. Then go down. Somebody has to see it done.\n\nUnder it, in Fennick's capitals: "AND WIPE YOUR FEET." And under that, very small, in the Director's own hand: "Whoever you are - I am glad somebody came. I could not pull either lever. I tried for nine days."
note baselocker Base locker | The base locker: rope, a lamp and a crowbar.
note statusboard Network status board | NETWORK STATUS (chalk, every line crossed out and rewritten in the same hand)\n\nSpirecrest Roofs: BEACON ON - leave it on.\nBrinelab: DARK. 02:14. (I am sorry, Mei.)\nBiome 1-6: DARK. Biome Seven: GREEN - Wren never listens.\nThalassa: SURFACE. Dives 41, 44, 47: cables cut.\nLumen Shelf: LIGHTS HALF - Lindqvist, please.\nCaisson Yard: DARK. Sluice 4. Eight men. Eight.\nHadal Commons: DOORS SHUT. DARK. SAFE.\nThe Hollow: - - - (no reading)\n\nIn the corner, a tally of five-bar gates. Forty-one. Each one, someone he turned the lights off on.
note pumplog Pump log | PUMP LOG - PUMP TOWER\n\nPressure's held for nine years on one crank a week. I sing to the crank. The crank does not mind.\nThe week the Commons' doors were open for the pumps, the pumps pulled something up the trench with the water. It came up the pipe like a cat up a curtain, and then it went back down into the Hollow, and it has been listening ever since.\nWe stopped cranking. The Director came down himself and stood here a long time with his hand on the wheel.\nCrank it now if you mean to RESTORE. Crank it anyway. Pumps want to work. So do people.
note warning Door warden's warning | DOOR WARDEN - G. FENNICK (pinned to the fuse board with a fork)\n\nThree fuses, three lockers. Set them and the spire lights up - and everything down there sees it. Everything. I mean the big one.\nIf you go to the Hollow, go when the lights are on. It hunts what is lit, but it cannot SEE in light, it can only find. In the dark it can do both.\nI am going down ahead of you to wedge the Hollow's gate. I have put the children on the plane. I have given Milo my hat. I don't need a hat where I'm going.\nIf you are the Stalker - you know the rest.
note networkmap The Network map | THE PELAGIC NETWORK - CONTROL ROOM MAP\n\nSeven stations round a ring, three wavy lines across it, and the Ringwave humming in the middle. At its centre, under the trench lip, one word: HOLLOW.\nPins in the map, one per station. Every pin but one has been pulled out and laid on the desk in a neat row, like teeth.\nThe last pin is on the roofs: SPIRECREST. A red thread runs from it out to sea, then curls back to the Hollow.\nUnder it, in the Director's hand: "Bait."
note inesmessage Ines's message | INES - IN PENCIL, ON THE DESK, OVER THE DIRECTOR'S PAPERS\n\nYou read it. Good. So did I.\nHe's gone down the trench after Fennick. Not to stop him. To help him, I think. I didn't ask.\nRESTORE turns the Network back on - the lights, the pumps, the doors - and the Commons can walk out. It will come up with them.\nSEAL drops the plug on the Hollow for good. The Commons stays in the dark, alive, for as long as dark lasts.\nI can't choose. I'd only choose Milo, and he's on a plane.\nTake Mo with you. He's been everywhere else.
note twoswitches Two switches | Two levers on the cable head, under glass, labels stamped in brass:\n\nRESTORE - power to every station, the doors on the cycle.\nSEAL - the plug over the Hollow, the Network dark for good.\n\nPull one. The other dies with it.\nScratched into the glass with a key, in three hands:\n"Lights." - W.A.\n"Quiet." - H.R.\n"Whatever you pick, then go down and finish it. Bring a lamp. - I.M."
note verdictrestore The verdict | RESTORE.\n\nAll down the cable, lights come on - station after station. Brinelab's windows, the domes, the Yard's red crane lamps, the shelf's five dots. Somewhere far below, great doors begin to move.\nOn the control room radio, the Director's voice, very tired: "There it goes. Every light I put out. They will come up now. So will it. Go down, and see it through."\nPull the descend lever.
note verdictseal The verdict | SEAL.\n\nThe cable jerks. Far below, something heavy drops into place. The lights on the cable go out, one after another, until only the Spirecrest beacon is left, far away, blinking.\nOn the control room radio, the Director's voice, very tired: "Quiet, then. Quiet for ever. I hoped somebody braver would pick the other one. Go down, and see it through."\nPull the descend lever.
note fuselocker1 Deck fuse locker | A locker on the door tower's deck: a fuse.
note fuselocker2 Tower fuse locker | A locker inside the door tower: a fuse.
note fuselocker3 Shore fuse locker | A locker at the door tower's foot: a fuse.
