prop sk_cavechest loot.refill=0
note sk_ruinnote Storm keeper's log | STORM KEEPER'S LOG\n\nThe radio on my table runs off the generator. The generator wants a part I lent to the cave crew, and the cave crew have not returned it, because they never return anything.\nWith power, the radio tells you where the last supply drop came down.\nI keep the weather for the Director. Every night he asks me the same question: "Is the beacon on the roofs still lit?" Every night I say yes. Every night he says, "Good. God forgive me. Good."
note sk_wrecknote Supply pilot's log | SUPPLY PILOT'S LOG\n\nLast run for the Spire, and the Director met me on the dock himself. No cargo, he said. Passengers.\nTwelve kids from the shuttle came up the trench lift with the door warden. I took all twelve. The warden would not get on. He said somebody had to go down and close a door properly, and he gave his hat to the small one with no whale.\nI flew them through the storm to the high island and came back for the crew, and the storm took the plane on the way in. I kept the crate. I would have kept the plane if it had let me.\nThey will decide it soon - RESTORE or SEAL. I am not staying to see.
note sk_wreckcrate Supply plane crate | The supply plane's crate: what the Spire ordered, never delivered.
loot sk_wreckcrate MetalIngot*2;Bolt*3;Rope*2;Plank*4
prop sk_wreckcrate loot.refill=0

# --- DEEP 1-HOUR (10-24): story items, notes and checks
story sk_key|Archive key|Hinge|The Network archive's key, from the chest at the bottom of the drowned archive.
story sk_crest|Kingdom crest shard|Bolt|A shard of the Sunken Kingdom's crest, from a drowned building. The Hollow's crown vault wants nine.
note skdeep Archive chest | The archive's sealed chest: titanium, and a crest shard.
loot skdeep story:sk_crest*1;TradeToken*2;TitaniumOre*2;CircuitBoard*1;OxygenBottle*1
prop skdeep loot.refill=0
note sklocker Storm Crown locker | The Director's own locker on Storm Crown.
loot sklocker TitaniumIngot*2;MetalIngot*3;Battery*2;Cooked_Potato*2
prop sklocker loot.refill=0
note sksumnote Sealkeeper's card | STORM CROWN\n\nFrom here I could see every station of the Network, one light each, like a necklace on black velvet.\nI used to come up here to count them. Then I came up here to count them going out.\nRESTORE or SEAL - the archive below remembers both, and it remembers me. Read it before you pull a lever. - H.R.
note skbldnote Archive register | NETWORK ARCHIVE - COMMAND REGISTER (printout)\n\nEvery band, every station, every call, and every remote command. The register does not forget. That is its job.\n...02:14 BRINELAB PUMPS LOCAL to REMOTE. AUTH: ROOK.\n...02:14 CAISSON SLUICE 4 OPEN. AUTH: ROOK.\n...THALASSA DIVE ORDERS 41, 44, 47. AUTH: ROOK.\n...LUMEN SHELF LAMPS 50 PERCENT. AUTH: ROOK.\n...SPIRECREST BEACON: HOLD ON. DO NOT EXTINGUISH. AUTH: ROOK.\nSomebody has underlined the last line twice, pressing hard. Ines, by the handwriting in the margin: "He kept it lit. He kept OUR roofs lit, so it would come to us."
note skledge Storm watcher's cache | A storm watcher's cache on a ledge of Storm Crown.
loot skledge Rope*3;Bolt*2;Feather*3
prop skledge loot.refill=0
note skcave2chest Archivist's spare chest | An archivist's chest at the back of the rock cave.
loot skcave2chest CopperOre*3;Rope*2;Battery*1
prop skcave2chest loot.refill=0
prop sksummit zone.id=sk_summit
prop sksummit zone.radius=2.5
prop sksummit zone.message=The top of Storm Crown. The whole island lies below.

